    {
      "id": "edge-endpoint-reassignment-instructions",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Interaction Contract",
      "position": {
        "x": -220,
        "y": 700
      },
      "width": 760,
      "height": 300,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 210
        },
        {
          "id": "top",
          "label": "top",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 270
        },
        {
          "id": "right",
          "label": "right",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 0
        },
        {
          "id": "bottom",
          "label": "bottom",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 90
        },
        {
          "id": "left",
          "label": "left",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 180
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "edge-endpoint-reassignment"
        },
        "markdown": "# Edge endpoint reassignment\n\n## Gesture\n\n1. Focus or select an existing edge.\n2. Grab its source or target endpoint.\n3. The opposite endpoint stays anchored and the selected end becomes a live tether.\n4. Compatible Ports become visible and labeled.\n5. Dropping on a compatible Port commits one atomic edge update.\n6. Escape, an invalid target, or a cancelled drop restores the original endpoint.\n\n## Invariants\n\n- Preserve edge ID, label, style, semantic role, and metadata.\n- Revalidate direction, datatype, and allowed edge types.\n- Never trigger a Port's drag-create behavior during reconnect.\n- Record one undoable transaction.\n- Support moving either source or target.\n- Keep a properties-panel endpoint selector as an accessible companion interaction.\n"
      }
    },
